  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let,&nbsp;<math><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></math> be vertical with height&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi></math>&nbsp;meters&nbsp;and at its end <math><mi>Q</mi></math> there is a balloon and <math><mi>P</mi></math> is on the ground<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>P</mi><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>P</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>P</mi><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>h</mi><mi>cot</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><msup><mn>60</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>h</mi><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mfrac></math><br /><math><mo>&#8756;</mo></math> <math><mi>P</mi></math> is the circumcentre of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#916;</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math> and its circumradius <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>h</mi></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/5e6537b4-383f-4163-965e-e1096c2cd33a.png\" style=\"width:1.96667in;height:1.71319in\" /><br />In <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#916;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math>,<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><msup><mn>30</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>2</mn><mfrac><mi>h</mi><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></msup></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><math><mo>&#8756;</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math> meters.",
